---
import MainLayout from "../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

// Puedes usar la misma imagen o una nueva que represente búsqueda/visibilidad
import blogHero from "../../../assets/rocko-legado.jpg";
---

<MainLayout
  title="Does your website speak the same language as your clients? | Otterock Blog"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-20 px-6">
    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <a
        href="/en/blog"
        class="inline-block mb-8 text-sm text-otter-deep font-bold hover:text-otter-accent transition-colors hover:underline underline-offset-4"
      >
        ← Back to Blog
      </a>

      <span
        class="text-slate-600 font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-xs mb-4 block font-body"
      >
        Digital Strategy • 4 min read
      </span>

      <h1
        class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-black text-otter-deep mb-6 leading-tight font-display"
      >
        Does your website speak the same language as your clients? (The truth about Keywords)
      </h1>

      <p class="text-xl text-slate-700 italic font-body mb-8">
        "Having a website isn't enough if no one knows how to find it."
      </p>

      <div
        class="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-12 aspect-video bg-otter-deep"
      >
        <Image
          src={blogHero}
          alt="Keyword optimization and digital visibility"
          width={800}
          quality="mid"
          format="webp"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-90"
        />
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed font-body">
      <p
        class="first-letter:text-5xl first-letter:font-bold first-letter:text-otter-deep first-letter:mr-2 first-letter:float-left"
      >
        Imagine you have an incredible hardware store. You sell the best hammers in town. 
        But on the sign at the entrance, instead of putting "Hardware Store", you put: 
        <strong>"Comprehensive manual impact solutions for solid surfaces"</strong>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Who is going to walk in? Probably no one. People search for "hammers", not 
        "impact solutions". Exactly the same thing happens on the internet.
      </p>

      <p>
        Often, businesses fail on the web not because their product is bad, but because 
        their page doesn't "speak" the same language as the people searching on Google. 
        Today at <strong>Otterock</strong> we want to teach you what Keywords are and why 
        they are the foundation of your digital success.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-otter-deep/10 my-12" />

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display">
          1. What are "Keywords"?
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Don't let the technical term scare you. Keywords are simply the exact phrases 
          your clients type into the search engine when they have a real need.
        </p>

        <div
          class="bg-otter-sand/50 p-6 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-otter-deep my-6"
        >
          <p class="text-slate-800 italic">
            "The client doesn't search for: 'Multidisciplinary legal service provider'. 
            The client types: <strong>'Divorce lawyer in Bogotá'</strong>."
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          Those words are the clues Google tracks. If your website doesn't have those 
          words strategically placed in its structure, you simply don't exist to the search engine.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12">
          2. The mistake of "Mute" pages
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Many agencies deliver visually beautiful pages, full of animations, but empty 
          of strategic text. They are "mute" pages.
        </p>

        <p>
          At <strong>Otterock</strong>, before writing a single line of code, we do 
          in-depth research. If you sell artisanal coffee, pretty pictures aren't enough. 
          Your page must explicitly tell Google: <em>"We sell the best roasted single-origin coffee in Colombia"</em>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12">
          3. Why does technology matter here?
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Even if you have the right words, Google needs to read them fast. Imagine 
          Google as a very impatient reader.
        </p>

        <p
          class="text-xl font-bold text-otter-deep text-center my-8 font-display bg-white/60 border border-otter-deep/10 p-8 rounded-2xl italic"
        >
          "In an Otterock website, the code is clean. We hand Google a perfectly 
          printed and easy-to-read book."
        </p>

        <p>
          Unlike generic templates that have "dirty" and heavy code, our <strong>Digital Craftsmanship</strong> 
          allows Google to understand your keywords instantly, giving you priority over your competition.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-4 font-display mt-12">
          Our 3-Step Strategy:
        </h2>

        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-center text-sm">
          <div
            class="p-6 bg-white border border-otter-deep/10 rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
          >
            <div class="text-3xl mb-2">🔍</div>
            <p class="text-slate-700">
              <strong>Research:</strong> We discover how your ideal client searches for you.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="p-6 bg-white border border-otter-deep/10 rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
          >
            <div class="text-3xl mb-2">✍️</div>
            <p class="text-slate-700">
              <strong>Copywriting:</strong> We create texts that convince humans and Google.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div
            class="p-6 bg-white border border-otter-deep/10 rounded-2xl shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow"
          >
            <div class="text-3xl mb-2">🚀</div>
            <p class="text-slate-700">
              <strong>Indexing:</strong> We make sure Google finds you and shows you first.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-otter-deep/10 my-12" />

      <section
        class="bg-otter-deep text-white p-8 md:p-12 rounded-3xl text-center relative overflow-hidden"
      >
        <div
          class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-white/10 rounded-full -mr-10 -mt-10 blur-2xl"
        >
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display mb-4 relative z-10">
          Is your business invisible on Google?
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-8 opacity-90 leading-relaxed relative z-10">
          Don't let your competition steal your clients just because they do speak their language. 
          At <strong>Otterock</strong> we create websites that are not only beautiful, but are also 
          found and sell.
          <br /><br />
          Want to know what keywords your business should be using?
        </p>

        <a
          href="/en/contacto"
          class="inline-block bg-white text-otter-deep px-8 py-4 rounded-full font-bold hover:bg-otter-accent hover:text-white transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-lg relative z-10"
        >
          Let's make them find you
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</MainLayout>
